    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n62449" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λεπίδ-ιον</span></b> , τό, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λεπίς</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>small plate, capsule</i>, used to close a tube, <i><span class="en">
				Hero
				<u>Spir.</u>
				1.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> a Syrian
			plant, <i>pepperwort, Lepidium latifolium</i>, used in cases of
			scurvy, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				2.174
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				12.58
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				13.350
			</span></i>:—in <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				3.119b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				9.385a
			</span></i>. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέπιδι</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέπιδ-διν</span></b> , τό.</div>
